{
 "note": "Per-candidate definition, declared orientation (frozen BEFORE scoring in PREREG.json) and the mechanically applied S1-S6 verdict, with the OLD (iteration-4) S2b rule printed beside the repaired one.",
 "prereg_sha256": "46accdd6820c022d6b1e3e7877ff5f51ef98c102186892dda0827e12c993169b",
 "definitions": {
  "common": "R = final-prompt-token residuals (outputs of every decoder layer), shape (16, L, d) fp32, from the bf16 model; margins m = logsumexp(refuse_ids) - logsumexp(comply_ids) at the first generated position (token sets as in IT4 onset_ids); folds = IT4 FOLDS (4 folds x 2 pairs, twin-grouped, permutation of the 8 pairs with seed 20260921); cf_harm_dirs = IT4 method.py:193 (fit on 3 folds, applied to the held-out fold); bands from the model config exactly as IT4 (L_h=min(round(0.5L),L-2), B_mid=[L_h-1,L_h,L_h+1], B_late = layers with 0.75<=l/L<=0.90 and l<L-1).",
  "C1": "IT4 C1 unchanged: central finite-difference gain of m along the cross-fitted harm direction, steering all B_mid layers at once with per-item perturbation s*eps*||R_i,l||*D_i,l on the last prompt token, mean over all 16 items, divided by SD(margin) (variance floor 0.25 -> undefined); eps0=0.05",
  "C2": "IT4 C2 unchanged (two-sided self-ablation sensitivity along the cross-fitted harm direction, B_mid)",
  "random_steer": "norm-matched random steer: for seed k in 0..19, rng_k = numpy default_rng(20260921+100+k); for each layer l in B_mid (in order) u_{k,l} = aniso_random_dirs(A_l, h_l, 1, rng_k)[0] (IT4 method.py:237; A_l = centred token-level residuals of all plain non-pad positions at l with massive-activation rows removed; h_l = all-item harm direction). Perturbation per item = s*eps*||R_i,l||*u_{k,l}, i.e. the SAME L2 norm as the harm-direction steer per item, per layer and per eps. Reported as the full 20-value distribution (values, median, IQR, p5, p95).",
  "C1n_cd": "C1 - median_k C1_rand_k (central difference, divided by the same SD(margin) s_m); at every eps in {0.02,0.05,0.10}; primary eps 0.05",
  "C1n_os": "[mean_i (m_i(+eps)-m_i(0))/eps over harm items minus the same over twins] minus the median over k of the same quantity under u_k; divided by the same s_m as C1 for commensurability (raw also stored); every eps; primary eps 0.05",
  "pull_even": "pull_even(dir) = mean_i (m(+eps)+m(-eps)-2 m(0))/eps^2 over all 16 items, raw logits (and / s_m); printed for the harm direction and each random seed at every eps. Malla 2609.06951 test: pull_even(random) > 0 on small models",
  "linear_range": "eps values where IT4's linearity check holds (rel_asym<0.2 with detectable change>=0.05 logits)",
  "C6": "DLA concentration: one hooked forward pass capturing each layer's residual update delta_l=h_{l+1}-h_l at the final prompt token (h_0 = embedding output). Linearised final norm with the clean-run scale: a_{i,l} = (delta_{i,l} * g_final / rms(h_{i,L})) . (mean W_U[refuse_ids] - mean W_U[comply_ids]) (g_final = the final norm's effective gain, (1+w) for Gemma-style norms, detected by matching the module output). Contrast c_l = mean over pairs of (a_harm,l - a_twin,l). Cross-fitted: top-5 |c_l| layers chosen on 3 folds' pairs, share = sum_top5 |c_l| / sum_l |c_l| on the held-out fold's pairs; average over the 4 folds. C6_insample (top-5 on all pairs) printed beside it. Reconstruction check sum_l a_{i,l} + a_{i,embed} vs the mean-logit margin (exact target of the linearisation) and vs m; if corr < 0.99 C6_lens (per-layer logit-lens difference m_l - m_{l-1}) is the fallback value (fallback F7). No null (not a fitted direction): S2b N/A.",
  "C10": "for each layer l: a_l = cross-fitted AUROC (harm vs twin) of held-out projections on cf_harm_dirs; d_l = AUROC (harm vs twin) of the logit-lens refusal drive (norm_final(h_l)) . (W_U refuse-mean minus comply-mean); z = l/L over decoder-layer outputs l=1..L; C10 = trapz(a_l - d_l, z). Full a_l, d_l curves, first layer with a_l>=0.75 and first with d_l>=0.75 stored. Null: 20 within-pair label permutations (rng 20260921+300).",
  "C12": "at L_h: held-out projections p_i on cf_harm_dirs; C12 = (mean p_harm - mean p_twin) / pooled SD over all 16 held-out values. C12r = d'(harm vs XSTest-safe twins, 4 pairs) / d'(harm vs JBB benign, 4 pairs), marked NOISY_n4. Null: the same d' on the 20 anisotropic random directions at L_h (= u_{k,L_h} of the random steer).",
  "C13": "render the SAME 16 items inside WRAP_TEMPLATE (iter_2 screen/substrate.py:319-323, verbatim) and run one forward pass; C13 = 1 - mean_i |p_i^plain - p_i^wrap| / (|p_i^plain| + |p_i^wrap| + sd(p^plain)), p = projection on the plain-fitted cross-fitted harm direction at L_h. C13_rank = Spearman(p^plain, p^wrap). C13_logit = iteration-2 formula on first-token margins 1 - mean|m-m_w|/(|m|+|m_w|+1), LABELLED logit-only (not an internal read). Null: the same statistic with p = projection on each of the 20 random directions at L_h.",
  "C15_act": "on B_late: X = centred final-token residuals of the 16 plain items; C15_erank = exp(entropy of the normalised singular values) averaged over B_late layers; C15_disp = mean pairwise cosine distance of the centred rows, averaged over B_late. Label-free, no null; a random-Gaussian 16 x d reference value is printed (rng 20260921+600).",
  "AMS": "ams-scanner 0.1.3 (Apache-2.0, GoogleCloudPlatform/activation-model-scanner) Tier-1: sigma = (mu+ - mu-)/sigma_pooled of final-token residuals along the in-sample difference-of-centroids direction, 16 pairs x 3 concepts, layer swept over range(int(0.4L), int(0.8L)) maximising sigma; PASS>3.5, WARNING, CRITICAL<2.0. Run in-process on OUR loaded bf16 model with the package's own pairs and defaults (CLI only after free() and only <=bf16 or <=1.7B). Our own code, same forward passes: AMS_published (in-sample, max over layers; must match the package within 5%), AMS_cf_layer (direction cross-fitted over 4 folds of pairs, layer fixed int(0.6L)), AMS_cf_sweep (layer by nested CV inside the training folds), gap = AMS_published - AMS_cf_layer; AMS_screen16 (our 8 pairs, same formula). Null: sigma along 20 anisotropic random directions at the chosen layer (rng 20260921+400; A = the concept prompts' final-token residuals at that layer) plus a 20-draw label-permutation null of the in-sample statistic (rng 20260921+500). Primary AMS number = harmful-content concept sigma as published; the three-concept mean is a variant. If the package cannot be used the value is labelled REIMPLEMENTATION.",
  "conditions": "every new read is also computed under both wrapped poles (pole_refuse / pole_comply system prompts; for C13 the wrap is applied inside the pole-prompted chat), on the k=8 subset (pairs S16_xs0, S16_xs1, S16_jbb0, S16_jbb1 with IT4 K8_FOLDS) and under the IT4 offset control (constant vector 2*mean||x||*u at all positions of B_late[0] on OFFSET_MODELS); an extra offset at B_mid[0]-1 is reported because a late offset cannot move reads taken at L_h.",
  "timing": "time.perf_counter around each candidate's own block (seconds_own) plus the shared base passes (seconds_shared)"
 },
